// D1572 — the VALUE of a `match` over an INTEGER scrutinee, at every delivery position and in
// both faces. Reported by the glean session as VL-020.
//
// Before D1572 the checker refused the scrutinee itself — `match scrutinee must be a union, got
// i32` — so every position was a loud check reject and the matrix's whole job is to show that
// admitting it did not leave a position behind. It should not, and the reason is structural
// rather than lucky: `desugarMatchAt` rewrites the arena slot to an if/else chain of `==`
// compares, so by the time any delivery position sees the node it is the hand-written if-chain
// those positions already carry, not a new node kind.
//
// The PROOF discriminates: `tag()` returns 2, so a cell that dispatched on the wrong arm (or
// fell through to `_`) prints something other than `two`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function tag() { 2 }
// @@VALUE@@
match tag() { 1 => "one", 2 => "two", _ => "other" }
// @@TYPE@@
string
// @@FALLBACK@@
"none"
// @@TEST@@
v == "two"
// @@HIT@@
print("two")
// @@MISS@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
two
// @@VALUE2@@
match tag() { 1 => "one", _ => "wild" }
// @@WANT2@@
wild
